# Function-like macros in WebGL shaders (cavekit-eaglercraft.md R2, T-666; engine patch 0122): render/goanna/test/
# jihad-webgl-macro.html compiles vertex shaders that define and invoke macros. UXP's Issue #2978 (2026-03) had stopped
# every function-like macro from expanding, so each failed with "'(' : syntax error" at its invocation, and with it
# EaglercraftX 1.8.8's first shader. Object-like and function-like, empty, with a body, with parameters, after #version
# and #line, EaglercraftX's own prelude: all compile; an invocation nested 300 deep in another's arguments is refused
# (the engine bounds the nesting at 256) and 20 deep compiles; #define D(x) x x nested 26 deep (2^26 tokens) is refused by
# the expansion budget (100 000 tokens a shader), quickly and without a crash.
id: webgl-macro
section: The engine
item: WebGL shaders with function-like macros compile (empty, with a body, with parameters, EaglercraftX's prelude); a 300-deep nesting and a doubling macro nested 26 deep are refused without a crash
shells: enyo mochi mojo
prefs: jihad.compat.trace=true
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-webgl-macro.html
kit: cavekit-eaglercraft.md R2
wait text done "rows 14" 60
probe rows '(function(){return document.getElementById("out").innerText.replace(/\n/g," | ");})()'
expect probe-has "c function-like, no params, empty: ok"
expect probe-has "e function-like, params: ok"
expect probe-has "j eagler's: ok"
expect probe-has "k nested 300 deep: FAIL"
expect probe-has "l nested 20 deep: ok"
expect probe-has "m doubling 26 deep: FAIL"
shoot rows
